---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
type Participation = { scope: string; dimension: string; group: string; label: string; n: number;
	modeled_voter_pct: string; modeled_nonvoter_pct: string; already_voted_self_report_pct: string };
type Flow = { prior_election: string; dimension: string; group: string; label: string;
	prior_choice: string; n: number; D_pct: string; R_pct: string; O_U_pct: string; N_pct: string };
type Margin = { prior_election: string; switching_pp: string; modeled_nonparticipation_pp: string;
	no_prior_contest_vote_entry_pp: string; other_or_unresolved_pp: string; denominator_pp: string;
	total_within_source_margin_change_pp: string };
const { names } = Astro.props as { names: Record<string, string> };
const data = 'data/participation-civic-estimates/20261108-01/';
const result: { participation: Participation[]; conditional_flows: Flow[]; margin_components: Margin[];
	conditional_flow_dispositions: { status: string }[] } =
	JSON.parse(readFileSync(`${data}output/summary.json`, 'utf8'));
const download = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`${data}output/download.json`, 'utf8'));
const release = 'https://github.com/hanshanley/margin_of_error/releases/download/participation-civic-estimates-20261108-01/';
const pct = (value: string) => `${Number(value).toFixed(2)}%`;
const pp = (value: string) => `${Number(value) > 0 ? '+' : ''}${Number(value).toFixed(2)}`;
const states = result.participation.filter(row => row.scope !== 'POOLED_SOURCE');
const pooled = result.participation.filter(row => row.scope === 'POOLED_SOURCE');
const overall = pooled.find(row => row.dimension === 'overall')!;
const dimensions: Record<string, string> = { AGE6: 'Age in the current study', RACETH5: 'Source race / ethnicity',
	EDUC: 'Education', SEX: 'Sex assigned at birth', GENDER3: 'Gender identity',
	INCOME: '2025 household income', RUCC: 'County urban / suburban / rural context' };
const prior = (year: string, value: string) => value === 'N' ? `No recalled ${year} contest vote`
	: year === '2024' ? (value === 'D' ? 'Recalled Harris' : 'Recalled Trump')
		: (value === 'D' ? 'Recalled Democratic House' : 'Recalled Republican House');
const withheld = result.conditional_flow_dispositions.filter(row =>
	row.status === 'withheld_sparse_source_joint_support').length;
---

<section id="participation-civic-estimates" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="civic-estimates-title"
	data-publication-class="exploratory-source-weighted-survey-model">
	<h3 id="civic-estimates-title">A voter-and-nonvoter study: exploratory 2026 estimates</h3>
	<p>NORC's Civic Health and Elections Project includes <strong>113,020 source respondents in all 50 states</strong>.
		Unlike the current-voter-only SSRS tables, this separate file also includes model-classified nonvoters.
		These are <strong>source-weighted estimates, not administratively observed turnout or measured staying home</strong>.</p>
	<p>The supplied weight's exact target, calibration and field period remain unqualified.
		“Pooled source” is not a certified national population estimate. Choices mix reported and intended votes;
		recalled past choices do not identify the full original electorate. No current response is reweighted to
		the old Trump/Harris split, and no design-aware confidence interval is invented.</p>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Pooled study-frame participation">
		<table><caption>Pooled source frame, not national turnout. Already-voted reports and model classifications differ.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Study frame</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter</th><th scope="col">Modeled nonvoter</th>
				<th scope="col">Self-reported already voted</th><th scope="col">Source n</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody><tr data-civic-overall>
				<th scope="row">Pooled source</th><td data-civic-voter>{pct(overall.modeled_voter_pct)}</td>
				<td data-civic-nonvoter>{pct(overall.modeled_nonvoter_pct)}</td>
				<td data-civic-reported>{pct(overall.already_voted_self_report_pct)}</td>
				<td>{overall.n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
			</tr></tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>All 50 state source estimates; D.C. not sampled</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All state study-frame participation estimates">
			<table><caption>Each row uses that state's respondents and native weights, not a national allocation.
				Source-weighted modeled participation is not certified state turnout.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter</th><th scope="col">Modeled nonvoter</th>
					<th scope="col">Self-reported already voted</th><th scope="col">Source n</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{states.map(row => <tr data-civic-state={row.scope}>
					<th scope="row">{names[row.scope]}</th><td data-civic-voter>{pct(row.modeled_voter_pct)}</td>
					<td data-civic-nonvoter>{pct(row.modeled_nonvoter_pct)}</td>
					<td data-civic-reported>{pct(row.already_voted_self_report_pct)}</td>
					<td>{row.n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
				</tr>)}
					<tr data-civic-state="DC"><th scope="row">District of Columbia</th>
						<td colspan="4">Not sampled; no estimate allocated</td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Broad demographic source comparisons and conditional choices</summary>
		<p>Current attributes are not fixed 2024 cohorts. Unknown and disclosure-removed attributes remain in the
			overall denominator, not recovered or assigned to named groups. Dimensions overlap and must not be added.
			The {withheld} sparse conditional rows stay withheld; source support is not a precision guarantee.</p>
		{Object.entries(dimensions).map(([dimension, label]) => <details class="explorer-notes">
			<summary>{label}</summary>
			<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${label} modeled participation`}>
				<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Pooled source group</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter</th>
					<th scope="col">Modeled nonvoter</th><th scope="col">Already-voted report</th><th scope="col">Source n</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>{pooled.filter(row => row.dimension === dimension).map(row =>
						<tr data-civic-demographic={`${dimension}:${row.group}`}>
							<th scope="row">{row.label}</th><td data-civic-voter>{pct(row.modeled_voter_pct)}</td>
							<td data-civic-nonvoter>{pct(row.modeled_nonvoter_pct)}</td>
							<td data-civic-reported>{pct(row.already_voted_self_report_pct)}</td>
							<td>{row.n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
						</tr>)}</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${label} conditional current choices`}>
				<table><caption>Percent of the full recalled prior-choice group within this current study frame.
					Not percentages of all original historical voters.</caption>
					<thead><tr><th scope="col">Group / recalled prior choice</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter, D House</th>
						<th scope="col">Modeled voter, R House</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter, other / unresolved</th>
						<th scope="col">Modeled nonvoter</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>{result.conditional_flows.filter(row => row.dimension === dimension).map(row =>
						<tr data-civic-flow={`${row.prior_election}:${dimension}:${row.group}:${row.prior_choice}`}>
							<th scope="row">{row.label} · {prior(row.prior_election, row.prior_choice)}</th>
							<td>{pct(row.D_pct)}</td><td>{pct(row.R_pct)}</td><td>{pct(row.O_U_pct)}</td><td>{pct(row.N_pct)}</td>
						</tr>)}</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</details>)}
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Within-source switching and participation components</summary>
		<p>The comparison holds the current source frame fixed: recalled 2024 President or 2022 House choice
			versus modeled 2026 House choice. It is not the observed national swing or causal persuasion.
			No prior contest vote is not first-ever voting, no prior ballot, or newly eligible status.
			Eligibility, death and migration remain unknown. Other and unresolved terms are combined here.</p>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Pooled source prior-choice current destinations">
			<table><caption>Full recalled prior-choice groups, including model-classified nonvoters.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Recalled prior choice</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter, D House</th>
					<th scope="col">Modeled voter, R House</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter, other / unresolved</th>
					<th scope="col">Modeled nonvoter</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{result.conditional_flows.filter(row => row.dimension === 'overall').map(row =>
					<tr data-civic-flow={`${row.prior_election}:overall:all:${row.prior_choice}`}>
						<th scope="row">{prior(row.prior_election, row.prior_choice)}</th>
						<td>{pct(row.D_pct)}</td><td>{pct(row.R_pct)}</td><td>{pct(row.O_U_pct)}</td><td>{pct(row.N_pct)}</td>
					</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Within-source normalized margin components">
			<table><caption>Signed known-major-party margin points; the denominator term is required for exact accounting.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Prior comparison</th><th scope="col">Switching</th><th scope="col">Modeled nonparticipation</th>
					<th scope="col">No-prior-contest-vote entry</th><th scope="col">Other / unresolved</th>
					<th scope="col">Denominator</th><th scope="col">Within-source total</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{result.margin_components.map(row => <tr data-civic-margin={row.prior_election}>
					<th scope="row">{row.prior_election} {row.prior_election === '2024' ? 'President' : 'House'} → 2026 House</th>
					<td>{pp(row.switching_pp)}</td><td>{pp(row.modeled_nonparticipation_pp)}</td>
					<td>{pp(row.no_prior_contest_vote_entry_pp)}</td><td>{pp(row.other_or_unresolved_pp)}</td>
					<td>{pp(row.denominator_pp)}</td><td>{pp(row.total_within_source_margin_change_pp)}</td>
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<p class="caption">Native weights are not people. Rounding can prevent displayed percentages from summing to 100;
		a displayed zero is not proof of no switching. No state survey estimate is allocated to counties or precincts.
		Complete permitted aggregate inputs, all selected queries, all withholding dispositions and exact calculation code
		are included in the download. Respondent records and original source documents are not redistributed.</p>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${release}complete-analysis.zip`} download data-civic-download="zip">Complete Civic aggregate analysis + inputs + code (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${release}participation.csv`} download data-civic-download="participation">All selected state / demographic participation estimates (CSV)</a>
		<a href={`${release}conditional-flows.csv`} download data-civic-download="flows">All selected conditional choice estimates (CSV)</a>
		<a href={`${release}margin-components.csv`} download data-civic-download="margins">Exact within-source margin components (CSV)</a>
		<a href={`${release}flow-dispositions.csv`} download>All conditional selection / withholding dispositions (CSV)</a>
		<a href="https://civichealth.norc.org/">NORC study</a>
	</div>
	<p class="caption" data-civic-archive>Complete ZIP: {download.bytes.toLocaleString('en-US')} bytes · SHA-256
		<code>{download.sha256}</code>. Attribution to NORC does not imply endorsement.</p>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-civic-estimates { min-width: 0; }
	#participation-civic-estimates code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
